-- e3_reach_fixpoint: Reach is closed under Init and Next.
--
-- TY SOUNDNESS META-THEOREM. `Reach Init Next` is the set of states reachable
-- by a transition system with initial predicate `Init` and step relation `Next`
-- — the exact state space TY's explicit-state model checker enumerates. We model
-- it as an inductively-defined predicate over an ARBITRARY state type `S`, with
-- an ARBITRARY initial predicate `Init : S → Prop` and step relation
-- `Next : S → S → Prop` (fully general, no fixed arity):
--
--   inductive Reach (S) (Init) (Next) : S → Prop
--     | rinit : Init s → Reach s                          -- every initial state is reachable
--     | rstep : Reach s → Next s t → Reach t              -- reachability is Next-closed
--
-- The two theorems below are the two intro rules read back as CLOSURE lemmas:
--   (1) e3_reach_init : ∀ s, Init s → Reach Init Next s
--   (2) e3_reach_step : ∀ s t, Reach Init Next s → Next s t → Reach Init Next t
-- Together they state that Reach is a FIXPOINT closed under Init and Next — the
-- soundness guarantee that TY's frontier BFS never leaves the reachable set and
-- always contains it. This companion confirms the `Reach` inductive elaborates
-- and that its constructors kernel-check as the closure witnesses.

inductive Reach (S : Type) (Init : S → Prop) (Next : S → S → Prop) : S → Prop where
  | rinit : (s : S) → Init s → Reach S Init Next s
  | rstep : (s : S) → (t : S) → Reach S Init Next s → Next s t → Reach S Init Next t

-- (1) Init-closure: every initial state is reachable.
theorem e3_reach_init
    (S : Type) (Init : S → Prop) (Next : S → S → Prop)
    (s : S) (h : Init s) : Reach S Init Next s :=
  @Reach.rinit S Init Next s h

-- (2) Next-closure: reachability is closed under the step relation.
theorem e3_reach_step
    (S : Type) (Init : S → Prop) (Next : S → S → Prop)
    (s : S) (t : S) (hs : Reach S Init Next s) (hn : Next s t) : Reach S Init Next t :=
  @Reach.rstep S Init Next s t hs hn